# `apps/` — Monorepo Applications

Each subdirectory of `apps/` is one application within the
{{.ProjectName}} monorepo. The expected structure for an app is:

```
apps/<your-app>/
├── AGENTS.md          # rules specific to this app
├── <source files>
└── <build config>
```

`AGENTS.md` is the only file aikata cares about; the rest is owned by
your stack (`package.json`, `pubspec.yaml`, `go.mod`, etc.).

## Adding a new app

Copy the `_example/` template and rename it:

```bash
cp -r apps/_example apps/my-new-app
$EDITOR apps/my-new-app/AGENTS.md   # fill in stack, test runner, etc.
```

`_example/` itself is excluded from convention-following tooling
because of its leading underscore. Do not delete the example — it is
the template that the next contributor will copy.

## Per-app rule scope

Rules inside `apps/<name>/AGENTS.md` apply **only when the agent is
working under `apps/<name>/`**. The repository-root `AGENTS.md` is
always in effect; per-app rules add to it without replacing it.

See [`docs/monorepo.md`](../docs/monorepo.md) for the full convention.
